flowchart TD
  %% Parallel Concurrent ESG Flow (conceptual, updated to reflect code changes)
  Start([Start]) --> LoadData["Load preprocessed reports / dataset"]
  LoadData --> Segment["Segment report into content chunks (semantic chunking)"]
  Segment --> Store["Index/store chunks for retrieval (ChunkStore) via chunk_store.put(report_id, chunks)"]
  Store --> Prepare["Prepare timing/logging (parse timing recorded; Timer.start/stop per domain)"]

  subgraph ParallelScoring [Independent domain analysts run concurrently]
    direction TB
    A1["Environmental analyst: retrieve top relevant chunks (PARALLEL_MAX_CHUNKS); estimate_domain_score; append RetrievalEvent to trace"]
    A2["Social analyst: retrieve top relevant chunks (PARALLEL_MAX_CHUNKS); estimate_domain_score; append RetrievalEvent to trace"]
    A3["Governance analyst: retrieve top relevant chunks (PARALLEL_MAX_CHUNKS); estimate_domain_score; append RetrievalEvent to trace"]
  end

  Prepare --> ParallelScoring
  ParallelScoring --> Collect["Collect independent domain scores and retrieval traces (trace contains RetrievalEvent entries)"]
  Collect --> Aggregate["Combine domain scores into a total score & aggregate confidence (aggregate_total_score, aggregate_confidence)"]
  Aggregate --> Evaluate["Compute evaluation metrics: coverage, hallucination, inter-agent agreement, latency, MAE/accuracy, deliberation summary"]
  Evaluate --> Compare["Compare predicted total to ground truth (error, direction, pct)"]
  Compare --> Result["Produce final run result (pattern=parallel_concurrent) with domain scores, traces, metrics"]
  Result --> End([End])

  %% Key differences: agents act in parallel (ThreadPoolExecutor controlled by PARALLEL_MAX_WORKERS), bounded retrieval per domain (PARALLEL_MAX_CHUNKS), lower latency but independent judgments
  classDef note fill:#f9f,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px;
  Notes["Key: parallel & independent; PARALLEL_MAX_WORKERS and PARALLEL_MAX_CHUNKS control concurrency & evidence breadth; retrieval_trace recorded"]:::note
  ParallelScoring --> Notes

